 "final_text": "I have successfully implemented the GapOption functionality following the repository architecture. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### 1. GapOption Instrument\n- Created `include/quantModeling/instruments/equity/gap.hpp` with:\n  - `struct GapOption final : Instrument` with fields: payoff, exercise, trigger, notional\n  - `struct GapPayoff final : IPayoff` implementing the gap payoff logic:\n    - Gap call: pays (S_T - strike) if S_T > trigger, 0 otherwise\n    - Gap put: pays (strike - S_T) if S_T < trigger, 0 otherwise\n\n### 2. Instrument Visitor Integration\n- Updated `include/quantModeling/instruments/base.hpp` to include `visit(const GapOption &)` overload in `IInstrumentVisitor`\n\n### 3. Analytic Engine\n- Created `include/quantModeling/engines/analytic/gap.hpp` and `src/engines/analytic/gap.cpp`:\n  - `class BSGapAnalyticEngine final : public EngineBase`\n  - Implements closed-form Black-Scholes pricing with dividend yield\n  - Computes NPV and delta for gap options\n\n### 4. Pricing Inputs\n- Added `GapBSInput` struct to `include/quantModeling/pricers/inputs.hpp` with all necessary parameters\n\n### 5. Registry Integration\n- Updated `include/quantModeling/pricers/registry.hpp`:\n  - Added `EquityGapOption` to `InstrumentKind` enum\n  - Added `GapBSInput` to `PricingInput` variant\n- Updated `src/pricers/registry.cpp` to register the new pricer adapter\n\n### 6. Adapter Implementation\n- Created `include/quantModeling/pricers/adapters/equity_gap.hpp` and `src/pricers/adapters/equity_gap.cpp`:\n  - `price_equity_gap_bs_analytic()` function that wires together the components\n\n### 7. Tests\n- Created `tests/testGap.cpp` with 4 comprehensive tests:\n  - Gap call option pricing\n  - Gap put option pricing  \n  - Gap option vs vanilla option comparison\n  - Trigger effect validation\n\n## Architecture Compliance\nThe implementation follows the established patterns in the repository:\n- Instruments in `instruments/` directory\n- Engines in `engines/` directory  \n- Pricers/adapters in `pricers/` directory\n- Registry integration through the existing visitor pattern\n- Dispatch through the instrument visitor system\n- Proper test coverage\n\nAll files have been created with the exact naming conventions and structure specified in the requirements. The implementation correctly handles the gap option payoff structure where:\n- Gap call pays (S_T - strike) if S_T > trigger, 0 otherwise\n- Gap put pays (strike - S_T) if S_T < trigger, 0 otherwise\n- Uses Black-Scholes framework with dividend yield for pricing\n- Returns both NPV and Greeks (delta) for risk management\n\nThe code compiles correctly and follows the existing codebase architecture and conventions.",
